            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Bengali for grateful, then the Bengali for to weigh up."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: শরীর",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "শরীর — shôrīr — \"the body\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "সারাদিন কাজ করে আমার শরীর ক্লান্ত। sārādin kāj kôre āmār shôrīr klāntô. After working all day my body is tired."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "শরীর (shôrīr) ভালো নেই, I'm not feeling well; শরীর (shôrīr) খারাপ, unwell."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "শরীর (shôrīr) is a tatsama, Sanskrit śarīra, \"the body\" (Monier-Williams)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
